{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/339783-what-is-your-abyssal-redemption-regimen","id":339783,"title":"What is your Abyssal Redemption regimen?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-14T00:05:36-08:00","id":339783,"title":"What is your Abyssal Redemption regimen?","content":"Say you were in charge of an NPC Abyssal's path to redemption. What sort of training or deeds would you do to get the Abyssal redeemed. Myself, since the Errata said that an Abyssal's redemption was partially dependent on gaining a profound insight to all 4 Virtues and Solar Exaltation, I would start off by training the Abyssal up to the Form charm of each of the Arguments of Virtue Styles as well as Solar Hero. Part of the quest would be to go back, if possible, to people from the character's mortal life and make amends for past wrongs. <br /> <br /> These are just some ideas that I have, and of course much more would be required. What ideas would you have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 12-14-2014, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T05:53:05-08:00","id":339943,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that you don't necessarily need dots in the Virtues to <i>understand</i> them: you don't need Valor 5 to get insight into bravery, especially if you've got buddies who are brave. It might not be so much buying Charms to enhance your Compassion as hanging around folks who are compassionate.<br /> <br /> Likewise with Solar Exaltation; that said, I might talk with the ST about the Unconquered Hero's Faith Charm, or if I was the ST, get it for the NPC and have him spend time observing the PC Solars using their Charms.<br /> <br /> If I wanted to dial up the epicness, I'd suggest that visiting the Unconquered Sun in person would help. A trip into Yu-Shan can be all kinds of fun for an Exalted game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T16:10:36-08:00","id":340275,"title":"","content":"1. Find (or be) an Abyssal interested in redemption.<br /> 2. Find Lunar Mate of said Abyssal, and convince him/her to help.<br /> --2a, Get Abyssal Laid in positive life affirming manner that does not induce resonance (using said Lunar Mate).<br /> 3. Teach said Abyssal Eye of Heaven Style (worship sun with violence...a good bridge)<br /> 4. Teach said Abyssal Arms of the Unconquered Sun style (Getting closer)<br /> 5. ???????<br /> 6. Profit<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I'M SORRY, I CAN'T HEAR YOU OVER THE SOUND OF HOW MANY MALFEAS CHARMS I HAVE!!!</b><i>~King Crazy Genius</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/345-kandagger","name":"Kandagger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T18:27:28-08:00","id":340312,"title":"","content":"I think looking at vtm's galconda would help a lot with this kind of thing, what kind of sacrifices and understanding it might take to completely transcend your state of being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T20:07:37-08:00","id":340408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/339783-what-is-your-abyssal-redemption-regimen?p=339943#post339943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that you don't necessarily need dots in the Virtues to <i>understand</i> them: you don't need Valor 5 to get insight into bravery, especially if you've got buddies who are brave. It might not be so much buying Charms to enhance your Compassion as hanging around folks who are compassionate.<br /> <br /> Likewise with Solar Exaltation; that said, I might talk with the ST about the Unconquered Hero's Faith Charm, or if I was the ST, get it for the NPC and have him spend time observing the PC Solars using their Charms.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Form Charms only require a score of 3, and Unconquered Hero's Faith requires Essence 4, and you don't want that if you are trying to turn back from darkness. You have to go on one hyper deadly quest per Essence dot, IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T22:15:57-08:00","id":340502,"title":"","content":"I would definitely require a meeting with the Unconquered Sun, complete with all the trouble that gaining entry into Heaven and access to the presence of the Most High should engender. Then, reciting your tale of woe in such a manner that he is moved, keeping in mind his ability to instantly know when you're telling the truth and when you've compromised your Virtues...<br /> <br /> If your tale moves him, he agrees to help you, although even he can't just outright reverse your condition. He kisses your bleeding caste mark, Endowing you with a seed of his Essence, which it is now up to you to nurture. At this point, I admit that I'm basically ripping off Promethean: You must build up the Solar essence within you by roleplaying your sincere devotion to Redemption, preferably by resisting the temptation of using your destructive charms, especially when doing so would benefit you greatly. When you have complicated your situation through these sacrifices, as well as reached other milestones by exploring your Virtues through positive actions, let's say as many times as you have dots of Permanent Essence, you roll your Redemption Pool.<br /> <br /> To make things really interesting, you may use your Whispers or current Resonance level as the Difficulty or as an Opposing Roll. If you succeed, then the Solar Essence blossoms within you (not unlike Doctor Who's regenerations), scouring away the taint of the Neverborn as you experience the agony and the ecstasy of rebirth into the Solar you always could have been. As an added consequence, not only are you a Solar untouched by the Great Curse, like canon says, but you also can &quot;sense&quot; the GC in others; you don't know what it is, but you can easily tell that *something* is seriously wrong with your fellow Exalted! Good luck convincing them of that, however...<br /> <br /> If you fail your roll, then the rage and hatred of the Neverborn surge forth and drown the sun's seed in the flood of their spite, and you suffer an immediate Resonance outbreak, Agg damage and gain a level of Whispers. If your ST is harsh, then that's it, you had your chance and failed. You can either adjust to eternal life as a Deathknight or commit suicide, which Ignis Divine is likely to help you with if he ever lays eyes on you again, courtesy of a Godspear to the face. Or, if she's lenient, she may allow you to try again, starting from scratch...<br /> <br /> That's pretty much how I'd do it. I also like the notion of the Abyssal going through the initiation Trials of Sorcery, specifically to learn Solar Circle Sorcery, and would roleplay that out as the &quot;exploring Virtues&quot; part above. But not every character would be that powerful or even sorcerously inclined, so that would be optional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T22:36:14-08:00","id":340532,"title":"","content":"For starters, I throw out the &quot;Must go on a quest per dot of Essence&quot; thing outright.<br /> <br /> Now granted, some ancient and blood soaked Abyssal Badass of Ultimate Darkness that's clocking in at Elder Essence would probably require considerably more effort to become a Solar than someone fresh off their Exaltation, but I really just plain don't like &quot;Must do this number of deadly quests to redeem, also getting stronger to better handle those quest means we tack on another one.&quot;<br /> <br /> Reminds me way too much of an MMO where you've got those <i>endless fucking fetch quests.</i><br /> <br /> Moving on.<br /> <br /> The way I look at things, the way an Abyssal becomes a Solar is entirely too personal to each individual to truly set anything down.<br /> <br /> That said, I've two guidelines for Abyssals, one looser than the other.<br /> <br /> The looser one is Unconquered Hero's Faith. Not so much for the access to Solar Charms that it grants, but rather for what the Charm represents. That no matter how deep the darkness is, there's a spark of light that will never go out. That, blackened and stained as you are by the Neverborn, you will not break, will not bow, and will not die on bended knee for them.<br /> <br /> The only thing that I really think is necessary though for an Abyssal, besides the desire to return to the light anyways*, is a reinvention of themselves, capped off with them choosing a new name for themselves. When they were chosen, when they took their Last Breath and Exalted, they cast their name in Oblivion. That name and who it represented? They're gone and they can't be reclaimed.<br /> <br /> Between your Exaltation as an Abyssal, what you've done since then, the trials overcome to be redeemed, and finally succeeding and becoming a Solar again, you are not who you were before it all began and you frankly never will be again. You aren't someone dreaming of a distant past that you cannot return to, but you are someone new with a whole future ahead. The new name chosen by the former Abyssal represents that and their conviction to move ahead and <i>live.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *I also apply the same in reverse. A Solar that becomes an Abyssal must truly desire it. They have to want, in their heart of hearts, to throw aside the Light of the Sun for the Darkness of the Underworld, and that can't be achieved by tossing a Solar into a magic torture box until they come out evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T22:46:31-08:00","id":340543,"title":"","content":"Great point about choosing a new name, I second that!<br /> <br /> But what about the Monstrance? The obvious thing is to have it blow up/melt down, but can we do something more interesting with it? What if it transforms into a home more suitable for a Solars' essence, a golden sarcophagus elegantly carved with idealized images of the newborn Solars' aspirations, and, instead of flying back to Lytek's cabinet, the purged Exaltation is truly free even of that restriction, and now returns unobstructed to its new base to set out from anew between lives...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T00:15:11-08:00","id":340611,"title":"","content":"Bad idea - the Monstrance counts as an arcane link to whoever bears its Exaltation, remember?<br /> <br /> Do you recall <i>The People of the Black Circle</i>? Or chapter 3 of <i>The Black Company</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T00:18:37-08:00","id":340635,"title":"","content":"Another important question to consider: what happens to those Abyssals whose appearance is deeply tainted by their exaltation upon being redeemed? Especially in the case of those Abyssals who go the low appearance route, and are little more than mummified husks or rotting monsters? A friend once suggested to me that it be a slow, rather unpleasant healing process but one that results in a body reborn in perfect, (though not necessarily beautiful), shape. It's an interesting question to ponder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>i don't know a hecking thing, my guy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4416-heedra","name":"Heedra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T00:21:43-08:00","id":340640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/339783-what-is-your-abyssal-redemption-regimen?p=340611#post340611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bad idea - the Monstrance counts as an arcane link to whoever bears its Exaltation, remember?<br /> <br /> Do you recall <i>The People of the Black Circle</i>? Or chapter 3 of <i>The Black Company</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not familiar...what happens in those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T06:18:03-08:00","id":340784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/339783-what-is-your-abyssal-redemption-regimen?p=340640#post340640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not familiar...what happens in those?</div> </div> </div> </div>A sorcerer gets hold of an arcane link to the character (interestingly enough a bit of hair both times), and uses it to seriously fuck the guy over.<br /> <br /> Except now you've got a giant-ass coffin that any sorcerer who wants to make a sorcerous ritual to screw your over with can target instead of having to get hair or toenails (which you can burn) or blood (which you'll at least be aware of them getting) or semen (I <i>hope</i> you're aware of them getting this from you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T07:37:37-08:00","id":340811,"title":"","content":"My take on redemtion requirements: (and its ok to get help with this)<br /> <br /> 1) Wreck your monstrance<br /> 2) get an audience and brutally invasive examination by lytek<br /> 3) get the UCS's blessing<br /> 4) with the UCS's blessing, go to the mouth of the void and denounce your allegiance to the deathlords and the neverborn<br /> 5) now go on a grand quest to each of the elemental poles to reallign your necrotic to that of the living (after this the abyssal enters a dangerous time where he no longer respires motes, but his mote-pool count as solar... but not done yet - your charms still work though)<br /> 6) Seek out Gaia's jouten - to primordially 'reboot' your body, so that it doesn't just die the moment the abyssal exaltation stops being an abyssal exaltation... (you did exalt split second before you would die, remember?)<br /> 7) Finally - without the use of charms or any supernatural means, accomplish a feat of selfless heroism worthy of a solar. This has to be done alone, and must be suitably heroic.<br /> 8) At the moment of finishing point 7, loudly and proudly declare what aspect of excellence your will strive towards as a solar (declare new motivation) - then you explode in golden light and become a solar<br /> <br /> During all of this, and especially after point 4, all the deathlords will be trying to kill you - if for nothing else then to prevent you from becoming a solar - because that might make other abyssals defect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T07:53:45-08:00","id":340817,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure about the second name part. Sure, that's a great way to go about it, building a new name untainted by Oblivion, and the Neverborn will be sure to strike you as if this fresh title were your old, but reaching into the maw of the Void and reclaiming the name you cast there speaks of the Abyssal's intent to reclaim both his Exaltation and himself from that same fate, and I like the poetry of it. The Abyssal should dedicate himself to be as the Solar he will become should be, a task made easier by the fact that the Great Curse does not affect him periodically (old Resonance rules). If you're using the newer resonance from Shards of the Exalted Dream, Abyssal players should always try to go for partial control, as opposed to willingly allowing Death to dominate their minds and actions, even for a moment. That is not to say that an Abyssal cannot kill; rather, he should make his killings according to the will of the Unconquered Sun, defending the innocent, slaying Creatures of Darkness primarily (or exclusively, sparing non-Dark creatures entirely), and offering the chance of surrender and mercy before finishing blows are made.<br /> <br /> There are several other aspects. Those who have had their appearance change (ex. the mummified husk guy earlier mentioned) might not heal from their wounds, the lingering 'wound' from their time in shadow. The Monstrance, if not destroyed, must at least be ritually severed from the Abyssal via painful thalmturgical rites or the Abyssal's offering of his own beating heart to the Unconquered Sun, freeing his next incarnation to pursue redemption in his name. Stopping a sizable threat originating from the Underworld using Solar-mirror charms from Unconquered Hero's Faith would certainly aid ny such quest. The only experience I have in the subject is my Dusk caste, Want of Nothing, adopting the pet name or his Sidereal love as his true name and willingly entering Heaven, knowing the Neverborn would more than likely strangle him to death on the steps of the Jade Pleasure Dome, to ask clemency from both Sol Invictus and said Sidereal. Confessing his love also seemed to help for some unspecified reason.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T07:55:58-08:00","id":340818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/339783-what-is-your-abyssal-redemption-regimen?p=340784#post340784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sorcerer gets hold of an arcane link to the character (interestingly enough a bit of hair both times), and uses it to seriously fuck the guy over.<br /> <br /> Except now you've got a giant-ass coffin that any sorcerer who wants to make a sorcerous ritual to screw your over with can target instead of having to get hair or toenails (which you can burn) or blood (which you'll at least be aware of them getting) or semen (I <i>hope</i> you're aware of them getting this from you).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Amanda Waller: &quot;All I needed to make my plan work was access to Batman's DNA. Fortunately, he'd left it all over town.&quot;<br /> Terry McGinnis: [shocked silence]<br /> Waller: &quot;Not even <i>remotely</i> what I meant!&quot;<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah, having a supernatural weakness like that is certainly supported by the myths Exalted draws from, and could be seen as a suitably heavy price to pay for being a redeemed Solar, free of the Great Curse. And it's not like you have to leave the thing laying around in the open! A Solar should be able to take extensive measures to hide his Monstrance in a very hard to reach place and/odd circumstances...like one of those Elsewhere Eggs, or a Pressed Beyond Time sorcery, or rediscovered FA spacial compression techniques to encase it inside of an enchanted walnut that she wears around her neck or buries near the Elemental Pole of Wood...<br /> <br /> In other words, if it's used to generate Story, it has a use for sticking around!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T13:37:26-08:00","id":341167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/339783-what-is-your-abyssal-redemption-regimen?p=340784#post340784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sorcerer gets hold of an arcane link to the character (interestingly enough a bit of hair both times), and uses it to seriously fuck the guy over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait...so THAT'S what someone taking a bit of hair from you means. Oooh dear...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But yeah, having a supernatural weakness like that is certainly supported by the myths Exalted draws from, and could be seen as a suitably heavy price to pay for being a redeemed Solar, free of the Great Curse. And it's not like you have to leave the thing laying around in the open! A Solar should be able to take extensive measures to hide his Monstrance in a very hard to reach place and/odd circumstances...like one of those Elsewhere Eggs, or a Pressed Beyond Time sorcery, or rediscovered FA spacial compression techniques to encase it inside of an enchanted walnut that she wears around her neck or buries near the Elemental Pole of Wood...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In other words, if it's used to generate Story, it has a use for sticking around!</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. For me, though I acknowledge that others may not feel so fond of this, playing Abyssals, ESPECIALLY the narrative associated with playing <i>repentant</i> Abyssals, has always been about dealing with and overcoming unique weaknesses and limitations. It's part of what makes it an interesting narrative to play. I, for one, think it would be kind of cool to see a newly redeemed Solar kind of have to develop a new relationship with that which shackled him during his time as an Abyssal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>i don't know a hecking thing, my guy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4416-heedra","name":"Heedra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T14:56:54-08:00","id":341246,"title":"","content":"I'm still not so fond of the idea of a thing made almost entirely out of soulsteel. i.e., the screaming souls of restless ghosts, turn from a conduit from which the dead Titans can wail their hatred at you to a solid-gold vessel to hold your Exaltation between incarnations, especially when the Exalatation is itself indestructible and nigh-irrepressible - why would you want it imprisoned when you die? And what happens to the ghosts that made up the soulsteel when your prison turns into a gilded divinity-sarcophagus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T01:55:10-08:00","id":341652,"title":"","content":"Not certain where I would start actually, but it would certainly be a chronicle long thing, and an extensive spiritual and physical journey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T07:17:34-08:00","id":341866,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, TUS takes you to Lytek, who opens a metaphysical door on your back, peers inside and goes &quot;Here's your problem...Someone's switched this thing to Evil!&quot; He flips a switch, BAM, Solar!<br /> <br /> Then, a hulking monstrosity, riddled with devil-body mutations and glowing green peeks around the corner:<br /> <br /> Infernal: &quot;Got room for one more?&quot;<br /> Lytek: &quot;Looks like I might have to put in a little overtime with this one!&quot;<br /> <br /> [everybody laughs the end]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T07:58:52-08:00","id":341885,"title":"","content":"A redemption path should be a path of atonement with the UCS. Atonement means to make an individual -at one with- their god. So the biggest part of this will be finding a way make yourself at one with UCS.<br /> <b>Step 1:</b> Save 10 lives for every life that you have taken in the service to the neverborn.<br /> <b>Step 2:</b> Find your Lunar Mate (may be done while working on step 1)<br /> <b>Step 3:</b> Take your soulsteel panoply and destroy it sending the souls trapped within to Lathe to be washed clean. Swear an oath to the sun not to use Soul Steel ever again.<br /> <b>Step 4:</b> Undergo Spiritual Purification, Abstance Fasting from food, water, violence, sex, pleasure, for an extended period of time and look outward upon the world. (This changes your virtues from there Abysssal nature to the way the Living understand them). This takes a number of days equal to your highest virtue<br /> <b>Step 5:</b> Spend 1 month in meditation, prayer and substistance fasting in a place a solar would meditate, and meditate upon the glory of the sun. Durring this time you can not prepare food, but can eat as much as 1 egg (with salt) per meal just enough to keep you going. You may have sex but only with your Lunar mate, if they are willing. The goal here to to focus your mind upon the glory of the sun and again away from you, to bring your soul and your exaltation into alignment with his.<br /> <b>Step 6:</b> Endure agony, and overcome death. What? You thought the fasting was the hard part? Hell no. You just called in the fire of the UCS to reignite your exaltation, child your soul feel like it's on fire as your burned from being a Creature of Darkness back to child of light. Your exaltation is free of the Neverborn at the start of this step...you just need to survive this...without the use of your charms. This will require an endurance check with a difficulty of your essence. Fail and the death you dodged bends you over the barrel, your exaltation goes free and finds a new host. Succeed and enjoy being a solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T08:22:49-08:00","id":341908,"title":"","content":"A redemption quest should work for the Exaltation, even if the current incarnation dies. All that effort, and the agony, and if you die everything doesn't matter? Seems like a very frustrating turn of events for a player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T01:16:56-08:00","id":342715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/339783-what-is-your-abyssal-redemption-regimen?p=341885#post341885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A redemption path should be a path of atonement with the UCS. Atonement means to make an individual -at one with- their god. So the biggest part of this will be finding a way make yourself at one with UCS.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, we will have to disagree. Atonement for many Abyssals will likely just mean making up to the world for the choices that they have made. Also, the Sun himself succumbed to the Games of Divinity and left Creation and Yushan to be destroyed during the Balorian Crusade, so until the Sun answers for his dereliction of duty, his non-partisans are justified in not caring about him. <br /> <br /> My method would look more like trying to emulate the change you want to see. Raise your Virtues to at least 3 because a Solar's Exaltation is derived from a god founded on those Virtues. Master Solar Hero Style so you can gain an enlightenment on to the nature of the Solar Exalted. Learn at least the Form Charm of Wood Dragon Style to harmonize your Essence and thought patterns to the way of life. Become an Exalted in tune with what he or she is trying to become.<br /> <br /> Note: On MAs, I read the Scroll book and it talks about how CMAs change you and your mannerisms, like how masters of Snake Style might be seen bowing to the snakes they see, recognizing them as teachers, or kill the snakes around him as reptiles are often given to killing each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T06:08:48-08:00","id":342849,"title":"","content":"Having all 4 Virtues at 3+ is going to be a pain in the neck, considering how going against one takes failing a roll and/or spending Willpower. It's also going to play all kinds of hob with one's character concept if that wasn't a direction you wanted to take the character - frankly, if my group had a cowardly Abyssal who wanted to become a brave Solar, that'd be one thing, but even then she doesn't want to become an <i>honest</i> Solar.<br /> <br /> One of the reasons I'm glad they're doing away with Virtues in Ex3 - <i>and</i> Hero Styles!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T12:27:55-08:00","id":343140,"title":"","content":"Abyssals as metaphors for fear, specifically fear of death:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>&quot;I dislike death, but there are things I dislike more than death, therefore there are occasions on which I will not avoid danger.&quot;</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> - Master Meng (Latinized as Mencius)</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">The stereotypical phobia therapy would be exposure treatment - gradually learning to face your fears, rather than back down from them. Having the psychiatric qualifications of a small table, though, I can't say whether it works or not.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">In the overall metaphor, that would be renegade Abyssals repeatedly coming face to face with their own potential deaths, enduring the hunt of their former colleagues - running up against the forces of death time and again - and eventually they realise: they're not afraid of it any more. If it comes down to dying, or watching others die, they'll hurl themselves in the way of a blade, smiling as they do so.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">And </span></span><i>that</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> is the moment golden light flares, and the Neverborn tremble in the depths of the Labyrinth.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T14:23:35-08:00","id":343273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/339783-what-is-your-abyssal-redemption-regimen?p=342849#post342849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having all 4 Virtues at 3+ is going to be a pain in the neck, considering how going against one takes failing a roll and/or spending Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just gives you more reason to develop a Cult. Not only does it give you a chance to stop drinking the Essence from the Underworld, it also helps you to manage one of the steps in your transformation. <br /> <br /> And I disagree with the notion that a less than all around virtuous Abyssal can shift into a less than all around virtuous Solar. To me, changing from an Abyssal to a Solar means being more Solar than the Solars. It means plugging up all of the wholes in your inner character where the darkness of the Black Exaltation lives and thrives. A SOLAR can get to be a douche like Havesh the Vanisher, both before and after Exaltation. An Abyssal who slowly kills the universe just by existing has to grit his teeth and do better. Maybe he can find a compromise that allows him to stay an Abyssal but manage his inner darkness, and not kill the universe and not be a Vanisher and just be a guy with some spooky powers. But if he wants to return to the light his Neverborn-twisted and defiled Exaltation, one that he earned by promising to kill the universe, he had better get ready to make some hard changes on the long road to Redemption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 12-17-2014, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T14:58:46-08:00","id":343313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/339783-what-is-your-abyssal-redemption-regimen?p=341908#post341908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A redemption quest should work for the Exaltation, even if the current incarnation dies. All that effort, and the agony, and if you die everything doesn't matter? Seems like a very frustrating turn of events for a player.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't help but disagree.<br /> <br /> The Exaltation is amoral. What matters is the person's intent. If you fail while walking the path to Redemption, I don't think some reservoir of &quot;Redemption points&quot; should be sitting around waiting for the next guy to take advantage of. <br /> <br /> It's only frustrating for the player if they inexplicably reroll the &quot;next holder of that Abyssal Exaltation&quot; and honestly if they still want to pursue a Redemption storyline, they probably need to start back in the Abyssal shit. It's a different character after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T17:08:13-08:00","id":343464,"title":"","content":"Lay one of the Neverborn to rest. Not as in '<i>Purge it to Non-existence with Fire!'</i> but, as in help it to find reconciliation with its end.<br /> <br /> Don't do this with a song that celebrates life, but with a grief-calling that honors the fallen. A funeral dirge that does necessary due to one of the fallen architects of Creation.<br /> <br /> To do this...<br /> The Abyssal unearths the secret history of Creation that was old when humankind was new, that it might write the incomprehensible name of the forgotten deity.<br /> <br /> It puts to rest the thousand shrieking, murdering Nephwrack's that colonize the Neverborn's skull.<br /> <br /> It brings the missive of strange devotion that was gasped out a dying primordial's maw, ten thousand years ago. It takes this message across impossible distances to deliver it to the ears of a Demon Prince who will weep to hear the impossible words, and swear eternal revenge on the Death Knight that dares to bring it to this humiliation.<br /> <br /> It burns in ritual a book of Necromancy born from the buried gods catacomb body; though Necromancy is lessened the world is perhaps made more safe.<br /> <br /> It travels to the chittering, clamorous, spiteful cities of the Aluan and brings a message of serenity to the Plasm-Creatures, and inspires them to take up rites and observances long forbidden since their time of death and exile.<br /> <br /> It gathers bits and pieces of a shattered being from these experiences, and a thousand-thousand more. It learns alien psychologies, it is twisted in body and mind a dozen times over and each slow recovery is achingly worse. It invokes names and prayers and benedictions that will mark it exile and <i>Nemesis </i>to a thousand heroes.<br /> <br /> It brings these thousand mournful-miracles to the lip of the Void, and in spite of the audacious impossibility of it all the Abyssal's Supernal-Sacred Requiem kindles a feeling of loss in the Neverborn that is less cold, deeper than its thousands of years of torment and anger. Where there was rage there is quiet, where there was horror there is rest. Perhaps even peace? <br /> <span style=\"color:#505050\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Datta. Dayadhvam. Damyata.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#505050\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Shantih shantih shantih</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe such a change does not destroy the Underworld, maybe it only <i>changes </i>it.<br /> <br /> The Abyssal that accomplishes this has done more for Creation than the +17,000 Exalted Heroes before them. It may be that the Abyssal is the only being in Creation that can do this, so close is <i>Death's Lawgiver</i> to the source of pain, rage and madness that make up the hecatomb bodies of that which cannot understand its death.<br /> <br /> This Abyssal has changed Creation irrevocably, it has opened up in the world a kind of peace, an absolution that shakes the foundation of what even the aged and mighty believe Creation to be. Such an Abyssal transcends the malfeasant power they wield and the foolish vows made at the rim of deaths door. Overcoming the <i>Horror-Seed </i>of their genesis, this Abyssal who must now be called something else. Would you call that individual redeemed? I can't think of a better term for it.<br /> .<br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> Oh. <i>Ooooh</i>, you mean how do Abyssals stop glowing black and start glowing gold? I dunno, spend enough XP on Solar-y things I guess? Whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":2711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","user":"Janissary87","date":".  cuzz I dislike bad grammar and I love flowery unnecessaries 12-17-2014, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T21:23:08-08:00","id":343663,"title":"","content":"What I would go for in a redemption path would depend very heavily on the particular Abyssal. I feel an achievement like this should be very personally guided, reflecting the character's conviction, laying to rest the mortal and Abyssal lives once led, and affirming the new life yet to be lived. Not to say some of the big, grand ideas in other suggestions can't feature, but completing them wouldn't be necessary or even the point in this approach. It's that the character takes up the path upon deciding that the deathly entity he is is less than the person he could be, and that he is not deterred from walking it, even upon finding how truly difficult and painful the journey is. I do like the bit about a better understanding of the Virtues, but I'd go more for TheCountAlucard's take; the character doesn't need to actually increase Virtues to gain that deeper understanding,* though it may be an appropriate step on the way.<br /> <br /> Whether a successful character manages to succeed and becomes a Solar, the Exaltation returns to the golden state it once held as the character passes into Lethe, or even the act creates or causes something entirely new... It's all down to the particulars of that story.<br /> <br /> * If asked to choose who was braver out of two characters consistently standing to face some supernaturally frightening things, one character with 5 dots in Valor and the other with 1 dot, I think I'd pick the latter in that situation. It takes a certain kind of courage to have everything about you screaming at you to run away (represented by probably failing the thing's supernaturally enforced Valor check with your 1 die) and then force yourself to stand up to it anyway (represented by spending that Willpower).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}